REASONS
- `evaluate_product_promotion` composition in [harness/build_soak/promotion.py](/var/home/dylan/projects/disclaude/harness/build_soak/promotion.py) is conservative against false-eligible cases: a run must pass `runs present`, `all runs PASS`, `no INVALID_RUN`, `no UNKNOWN_FAILURE`, and provider checks before eligibility can be true.
- The eligibility calculation is effectively “eligible iff no check is `False`” while preserving informational checks (`ok is None`), matching bakeoff-style convention used in [harness/build_soak/bakeoff.py](/var/home/dylan/projects/disclaude/harness/build_soak/bakeoff.py).
- Default posture is correct for HARN-1b dependency gating: when `require_product_harness=False`, product harness appears as `ok=None` and does not block, while setting it True enforces the sub-gates as blocking (`False` on missing/failed sub-gate).
- Tests in [harness/build_soak/tests/test_promotion.py](/var/home/dylan/projects/disclaude/harness/build_soak/tests/test_promotion.py) exercise the stated scenarios and confirm the check-shape and blocking behavior.

